# DevSecOps + AppSec

Source: [awesome-cursorrules security-devsecops-ssdls-appsec.mdc](https://github.com/PatrickJS/awesome-cursorrules/blob/main/rules/security-devsecops-ssdls-appsec.mdc)

## General

- Never hardcode secrets, tokens, or API keys — use env / vaults
- Do not commit `.env`, private keys, or unknown tokens
- Never log secrets, session tokens, or OAuth codes
- Validate and sanitize user input; escape output in HTML/JS/SQL contexts
- Avoid `eval` / unsafe dynamic execution

## Database

- Parameterized queries only — no SQL string concatenation
- Least privilege for DB users

## Dependencies

- Only packages from verified sources
- Do not add dependencies without explicit approval and a quick security glance
- Prefer pinning versions in `requirements.txt`

## AuthZ

- Enforce least privilege for admin / premium / chat-manage checks already in the bot
- Do not weaken existing permission gates for convenience
